      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Find the exact solution of the equation $2^{x}=3.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We take $\\log_{2}$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2^{x}&=3\\\\\\log_{2}(2^{x})&=\\log_{2}(3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that $\\log_b(b^c)=c$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives:\n\n$$\nx=\\log_{2}(3).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\log_{2}(3)$.",
