    "question": {
      ":question/id": "6ce71057-3b93-57ed-9c76-e4fd2c811395",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Find the exact solution of the equation $7^{x-2}=3.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we take $\\log_{7}$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7^{x-2}&=3\\\\\\log_{7}(7^{x-2})&=\\log_{7}(3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that $\\log_b(b^c)=c$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives:\n\n$$\nx-2=\\log_{7}(3).\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-2&=\\log_{7}(3)\\\\x&=\\log_{7}(3)+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\log_{7}(3)+2$.",
